\* All TLC check configs for AntflyQueryCompleteness.tla, one section per check.
\* Sections are verbatim TLC config syntax; the build extracts them
\* (scripts/tla-cfg.sh). Section names match the make-target check ids.

==== positive tier=fast
CONSTANTS
  BuggyRouteBeforeChildReady = FALSE
  BuggyDoubleServe = FALSE
  BuggyDropMovedDoc = FALSE

SPECIFICATION Spec

INVARIANTS
  TypeOK
  NoMissingDocs
  NoDuplicateDocs
  RouteRequiresChildServing
  Safety

==== BadDoubleServe
\* Expected-failure config for AntflyQueryCompleteness.tla.
\* The parent keeps scanning the moved right range after child routing is visible.

CONSTANTS
  BuggyRouteBeforeChildReady = FALSE
  BuggyDoubleServe = TRUE
  BuggyDropMovedDoc = FALSE

SPECIFICATION Spec

INVARIANTS
  NoDuplicateDocs

==== BadMissingDoc
\* Expected-failure config for AntflyQueryCompleteness.tla.
\* The child publishes serving without the moved document, so routing is ready
\* but the query result misses the moved range's document.

CONSTANTS
  BuggyRouteBeforeChildReady = FALSE
  BuggyDoubleServe = FALSE
  BuggyDropMovedDoc = TRUE

SPECIFICATION Spec

INVARIANTS
  NoMissingDocs

==== BadRouteBeforeChildReady
\* Expected-failure config for AntflyQueryCompleteness.tla.
\* A route to the child can publish before the child has a complete serving view.

CONSTANTS
  BuggyRouteBeforeChildReady = TRUE
  BuggyDoubleServe = FALSE
  BuggyDropMovedDoc = FALSE

SPECIFICATION Spec

INVARIANTS
  RouteRequiresChildServing
